# The one ONNX Runtime pin (57 §6 step 2c): the version every ONNX model in the daemon
# runs on (Parakeet TDT, Nemotron streaming, TEN-VAD, pyannote/wespeaker, laya), fetched
# from github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/releases by package-macos.sh (bundled into the .app)
# and release-models.sh (published per platform to the model bucket; the Linux desktop app
# downloads its copy from there, package-linux.sh bundles none). Bumping: change
# ORT_VERSION, refresh every sha256 (`shasum -a 256 onnxruntime-<platform>-<version>.tgz`),
# and re-run both scripts. Keep `ort` in Cargo.toml compatible (rc.13 wants ≥ 1.17).
ORT_VERSION="1.27.0"
ORT_SHA256_OSX_ARM64="545e81c58152353acb0d1e8bd6ce4b62f830c0961f5b3acfedc790ffd76e477a"
ORT_SHA256_LINUX_X64="547e40a48f1fe73e3f812d7c88a948612c23f896b91e4e2ee1e232d7b468246f"
ORT_SHA256_LINUX_AARCH64="3e4d83ac06924a32a07b6d7f91ce6f852876153fc0bbdf931bf517a140bfbe48"
# Design 58 fills this when Windows builds ship:
# ORT_SHA256_WIN_X64=""      # onnxruntime-win-x64-${ORT_VERSION}.zip
